From 82717b3379f439603de6b0c19c6294ca3097f2e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:18:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(input): a CDP press goes to the element under the pointer
 and focuses as Chrome does

Mouse events went to document.elementFromPoint, which page script can
replace, falling back to whatever element was last scrolled to, focused or
measured (__obscura_click_target, set as a side effect of
getBoundingClientRect). A press then focused the nearest ancestor matching a
hard-coded selector list, so a click often focused the outer container.

Mouse events now go to the renderer's hit target (__obscura_hitTarget), the
click to the nearest flat-tree common ancestor of press and release, and a
press nobody cancelled runs the HTML mouse-focus rule. Keys and inserted text
go to the focused element even inside a shadow tree, with composed
InputEvents. The click-target fallback is gone, and DOM.scrollIntoViewIfNeeded
scrolls only when the element is not fully in view, centring it, as Chrome
does. Tests that steered input by overriding elementFromPoint now press where
the element is laid out.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
